@page
@model CybersecurityTrainingApplication.Web.Pages.ResultsModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Assessment submitted"; }

<main class="results-workspace">
    <section class="results-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Assessment submitted</span><h1>Your responses are ready for marking</h1><p>Module @Model.ModuleId · @Model.ModuleTitle · Assessment set assigned automatically</p><div class="results-hero__stat"><strong>@Model.Answered</strong><span>of 10 responses recorded in this frontend preview</span></div></section>
<div class="results-grid"><section class="results-card"><span class="eyebrow">What happens next</span><h2>Secure server-side marking</h2><p>The final score, answer explanations, result status and attempt record must be calculated and stored by the backend. This prevents the browser from deciding a learner’s score.</p><div class="results-card__note"><span aria-hidden="true">i</span><p>When Ankit and Samuel connect the assessment service, this screen will receive the real score, assigned-bank history and personalised feedback automatically.</p></div></section><aside class="results-card results-card--details"><h2>Attempt summary</h2><dl><div><dt>Module</dt><dd>Module @Model.ModuleId</dd></div><div><dt>Assessment bank</dt><dd>Assigned automatically</dd></div><div><dt>Responses completed</dt><dd>@Model.Answered of 10</dd></div><div><dt>Marking status</dt><dd>Pending backend connection</dd></div></dl><a class="btn btn-primary w-100" asp-page="/Module" asp-route-id="@Model.ModuleId">Return to module</a><a class="results-link" asp-page="/Assessment" asp-route-moduleId="@Model.ModuleId">Start another attempt</a></aside></div>
</main>
